    <statement><p>Suppose that <m>a</m>, <m>b</m> and <m>c</m> are 
the sides of a right triangle, where side <m>a</m> 
is across from angle <m>A</m>, side <m>b</m> is across 
from angle <m>B</m>, and side <m>c</m> is across from 
the right angle.  If <m>a = 17</m> and <m>B = 33^{\circ}</m>, 
find the missing sides and 
angles in this right triangle.  
All angles should be in degrees (not radians), and  
all trig functions entered will be evaluated in degrees 
(not radians).</p>
<p>(a) Side <m>b</m> = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) Side <m>c</m> = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>(c) Angle <m>A</m> = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/> degrees</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>17\tan\mathopen{}\left(33\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{17}{\cos\mathopen{}\left(33\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>90-33</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
  </static>
